---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Stamp from "../components/Stamp.astro";
import rosette from "../ornaments/rosette.svg?raw";
---
<Base
  title="cartouche — maps made by asking"
  description="Cartouche turns a plain request into a map recipe and renders plates in styles borrowed from real cartography. In progress; no download yet."
  ogImage="/og/cartouche.jpg"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 pt-12">
    <p class="stamp-text text-ink-soft">tools</p>
    <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
      <h1 class="text-[2.2rem] leading-none text-ink-deep">Cartouche</h1>
      <Stamp label="in progress" />
    </div>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-[1.15rem]">
      A mapping tool that makes maps the way you'd ask Eratosthenes to make you one.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl">
      Cartouche turns a plain request into a map recipe — layers, styles, labels — and
      renders plates in styles borrowed from real cartography: engraved atlas sheets,
      transit diagrams, topographic surveys. An agent helps translate intent into recipes,
      but the renderer stays procedural and inspectable, so what comes out is a recipe you
      can edit, not a picture you can't.
    </p>

  </div>

  <figure class="relative mx-auto mt-12 w-full max-w-[1150px]">
    <div
      class="ornament pointer-events-none absolute -right-10 -top-10 hidden w-40 text-ink opacity-[0.07] md:block"
      aria-hidden="true"
      set:html={rosette}
    >
    </div>
    <img
      src="/plates/batavia-cartouche.webp"
      width="1150"
      height="504"
      alt="Engraved title cartouche from an 18th-century plan of Batavia, with figures and lettering"
      class="block h-auto w-full"
      loading="lazy"
    />
  </figure>
  <div class="mx-auto mt-3 max-w-4xl px-6">
    <p class="stamp-text text-ink-soft">
      a cartouche — the ornamental frame around a map's title — from an 18th-century plan of batavia
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6">
    <section class="mt-16 max-w-2xl">
      <h2 class="text-[1.5rem] text-ink-deep">Status</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        There's no download yet, and nothing is public. When there is, the installer and
        the repository will appear here — not before.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4">
        The first styles being built are the engraved sheet (this site's own plate
        language), a schematic transit style, and a clean survey style for print. Maps get
        a scale bar and a north arrow because a map without them is a drawing.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
